Comment:
 src/p25p2mac.c (lengths of the Phase 2 MAC structures, field positions of
 the multi-fragment messages) and src/p25alias.c (Motorola talker alias
 table) hold tables after sdrtrunk, Copyright Dennis
 Sheirer, and OP25, Copyright Max H. Parke KA1RBI, Graham J. Norbury and
 others, both GPL-3.0+; each is credited beside the table. The DMR sources
 likewise hold tables and layouts as sdrtrunk and OP25 have them, each
 credited beside it: src/dmrfec.c (Hamming generator matrices, CACH bit
 positions, block product code layouts, RS(12,9), CRC masks), src/dmrtypes.c
 (sync words), src/dmrmsg.c (link control, talker alias and burst
 layouts), src/dmrcsbk.c (the CSBK opcode table and message layouts),
 src/dmrdata.c and src/dmrdataapp.c (packet data header, block and
 application layouts) and src/dmrchan.c (the rule for choosing the station
 family automatically). src/dmrmsg.c (the Hytera XPT channel grant layout)
 and src/dmrdata.c (the Motorola MNIS CRC span) follow DSD-FME and dsd-neo,
 ISC, Copyright lwvmobile and arancormonk.

